invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_square multiplies a_i by word i + 1 of 2a, which
  holds the top bit of a_i, where V_i holds a_{i+1} shifted up one bit and
  no bit of a_i: a square whose word i has its top bit set is then wrong.
  bin/rsa_equiv_test holds the square to the multiplication of the number
  by itself.

--- old
            ct_u128 ab = ct_mul128(*a_word, a[i + 1] << 1) + t[i + 1] + ab_carry;
--- new
            ct_u128 ab = ct_mul128(*a_word, d[i + 1]) + t[i + 1] + ab_carry;
